  "notes": "USAGE:\n- 〜が{疎|うと}ましい (to find ~ disagreeable)\n- {疎|うと}ましく{思|おも}う (to think of as unwelcome)\n- {疎|うと}ましげな (with a distasteful manner)\nExpresses a feeling of wanting to keep distance from something unpleasant. Stronger than mere dislike—suggests an instinctive aversion.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {疎|うと}い (estranged, unfamiliar - related root)\n- {煩|わずら}わしい (troublesome, annoying)\n- {厭|いと}わしい (detestable)",
